'''Imfezzan''' '''Baliscans''' or '''Ifezzan Baliscans''' ({{Lang-bl|Fezanés Baliscanos}}; {{Langx|ber|ⵉⵎⴼⴻⵣⵣⴰⵏ ⵉⴱⴰⵍⵉⵙⴽⴰⵢⴻⵏ|Imfezzan Ibaliskayen}}) are [[Baliscans]] of predominantly [[W:Berbers|Fezzan ancestry]]. They are a subgroup of [[Kafto-Baliscans]], and the [[Northern Kafto-Baliscans|Northern Kafto-Baliscan]] subgroup. Fezzan-speaking people from [[Sudanese Kaftia|the Sudan]] arrived in [[Balisca]] as early as the beginning of the 16th century as part of the [[Ethiopian slave trade]], during the [[Colonial Balisca|colonization of Balisca]].  

